    "turn_text": "The state senator, GOP state senator, state senate nominee, pardon me, Kyle Kohler, had some information. So you know Kyle, he's pointed out a couple of things I'll just bring up to your attention here. Haitian migrants are given anywhere from 600 to 1600 bucks a month. through the refugee cash assistance program uh... landlords there know this and they are exploiting these migrants with high rents and uh... temp agencies there keeping them in part-time jobs i see the local schools there are overrun they've got over sixteen hundred non-english speaking students requiring the hiring of costly translators there. And I'm seeing that some of these students that are going to high schools in Springfield, these Haitian migrants, some of them are 19, 20 years old. They're in classes with freshmen students who are 14, 15 years old. That seems like a huge problem to me. I'm not blaming the migrant, the Haitians here. They want a better life, but the system is broken, Mike.",
